course: dictionary
lesson: 9559
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word stout can describe a thing, a person, or a feeling, and it can even name a drink. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: «He wore stout boots for the muddy hill walk.» Boots that can handle mud must be thick and strong, so stout means strong and thick here. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «He wore strong, thick boots» still makes sense.
explain: «Toad is a short, stout figure» describes the body of a character, so stout means rather fat or heavy. This is a polite word for it, and some people now think it is old-fashioned. Kind words for bodies include curvy and cuddly.
explain: «The stout defender stood firm in front of the goal.» Here stout means brave and firm. Stout can also be a noun: a stout is a strong, very dark beer. The sentence tells you which meaning you need, so always read on before you decide.
fact: Stout is an adjective, so it describes a noun, and it can change to stouter and stoutest.
fact: «Stout» means strong and thick, as in stout boots or a stout stick.
fact: «Stout» means brave and firm, as in a stout defender or a stout heart.
fact: «Stout» can mean rather fat or heavy in body; it is a polite but old-fashioned word.
fact: As a noun, «stout» means a strong, very dark beer.
exercise: «The Rat chose a stout stick for his walk.» What does stout mean here? | *Strong and thick | A dark beer | Rather fat | Very quiet
exercise: «The stout defender stood firm in front of the goal.» What does stout mean here? | Strong and thick like boots | Rather fat | Very dark in colour | *Brave and firm
exercise: Which word means a strong, very dark beer? | Stoutly | *Stout | Stouter | Stoutest
test: «Toad is a short, stout figure, splashing badly and rolling a good deal.» In this sentence, stout means? | A strong, very dark beer | Strong and thick | *Rather fat or heavy in body | Brave and firm
test: Which phrase uses stout to mean brave and firm? | *Stout heart | Short and stout | Stout stick | Stout boots
exam: Dad says «Pack a stout stick for the hill walk.» Which meaning fits best? | *Strong and thick | A strong, very dark beer | Brave and firm | Rather fat or heavy in body
